WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.680
The Sikh scripture runs to 1,430 pages.

2
00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:07.580
And it is poetry, meant to be sung.

3
00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:12.410
Its hymns are arranged by 31
musical modes, called raags.

4
00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:17.140
The earliest surviving collection
of its hymns dates from the 1570s.

5
00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:19.600
So who wrote the Sikh scripture?

6
00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:23.140
And why do scholars argue
about how it was put together?

7
00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:26.390
In this mission, you'll trace how
the scripture was put together,

8
00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:28.230
stage by stage.

9
00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:31.200
Then you'll meet a historian
of early manuscripts,

10
00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:34.560
and a body of Sikh scholars
who challenge his method.

11
00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:38.010
Your mission: find out who
wrote the Sikh scripture,

12
00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:41.090
and why scholars argue about
how it was put together.
